@[kernel step]
Install at least one kernel. The choices (each has its own instructions):

  @[todo iso-kernel]      the kernel this ISO runs: copied over in a minute,
                        works on this machine now
  @[todo compile-kernel]  your own: the linux spell (sorcery builds and keeps
                        track of it) or one you build by hand

Both together is fine too: the ISO kernel to boot right away, your own one
later. Only a kernel from the linux spell is tracked by sorcery (updated
with the rest of the system, removed by dispel); the ISO kernel and a
hand-built one are files you look after yourself.

To see these instructions again, type @[todo]. When you have a kernel
installed, type @[next] to go on to the boot loader.
